PW grand-canonical SCF prototype on a six-atom Li slab with PCC 2D and
Fermi-Dirac smearing. The electron count is allowed to relax toward a fixed
target work function. The test uses two Gaussian counter-charge sheets rather
than the multipole PCC 2D correction. It also checks the analytic
ion-counter-charge force in the SCF force path. The work-function reference
uses the CP2K convention: the planar average on the outer grid plane along the
open cell direction. Stress is evaluated from central strain derivatives of
the Gaussian counter-charge energy.
